{#
  The Kentenich-text edit form — the Twig counterpart of
  module/Books/view/books/texts/edit.phtml and its fields-partial.phtml, which still
  render this page wherever laminas is the front controller.

  Field order is that partial's, in its order, and should be changed in both or
  neither: the two renderings are live at the same time on different front
  controllers, and a moderator who edits a text through one and then the other should
  not see the form rearrange itself.

  Unlike the association form, every field here goes through a plain row — the partial
  builds no groups by hand — so this template is the shape most of batch 7's ten take.
  `security` (the CSRF token) and `kind` (a hidden input) are rendered through
  `form_row` exactly as the partial does, and App\Form\BootstrapFormRenderer::row()
  answers both by emitting the bare element with no form-group around it, which is what
  TwbBundle does.

  **The field rows live in `books/_text-fields.html.twig` now**, shared with the create
  form so that a field cannot be added to one surface and quietly forgotten on the
  other. What stays in this file is what edit.phtml keeps outside its own partial —
  which is not the same set for every entity, and is the detail worth checking before
  moving anything across the boundary.
#}
{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{#
  The two assets fields-partial.phtml appends through headLink()/headScript(). The
  script filename carries the primary language because the bundle contains the
  jQuery-validate locale strings.
#}
{% block page_stylesheets %}
        <link href="/css/gen-selectize-markdown-jquery-ui.css" media="screen" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css">
{% endblock %}

{% block page_scripts %}
        <script src="/js/gen-validate-selectize-markdown-{{ current_language() }}.js"></script>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<h1>{{ translate(page_title) }}</h1>

{{ form_open(form, form_action) }}
{{ include('books/_text-fields.html.twig') }}
{{ form_close() }}
{% endblock %}

{% block inline_scripts %}
{#
  selectize on the tag list, and the `[]` in the selector is not a typo: `tags` is a
  multiple select, so its name really is `tags[]` in the markup. Batch 5 found the
  renderer dropping that suffix on a different form, which submitted one value where
  the visitor had picked several — so this selector is also an assertion that it is
  still there.
#}
<script nonce="{{ csp_nonce() }}">
$(function () {
$("select[name='tags[]']").selectize({
    create: true,
    sortField: 'text'
});
});
</script>
{% endblock %}
